#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

NumPy: broadcasting `[[0,2,4],[3,5,7]]`, shape `2,3`, element `7`, total
`21`, strided slice sum `10` (`row[0:3:2]` is `[3,7]`; dropping the stride
and summing the whole row gives `15`), mean `3.5`. The arrays stay on the
Python side; Auto only extracts the six small values. `shape` is an
attribute-derived object, indexed by int; `row` is indexed by a Python
`slice` object.

`json`: text-key indexing (`data["values"]`), nested leaf reads, keyword
arguments, Unicode serialization (`ensure_ascii: false`) and the structural
round trip — encoding the decoded tree again yields the same fixed UTF-8
text. The `value:0` line is the A2PY run-observation channel, not output.

## Case: numpy-shape-error-caught
id: "py.libraries.1126.numpy-shape-error-caught"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1126"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.as"
syntax: "auto-script"

```auto
use.py numpy: arange
fn main() int {
    var caught = 0
    try { var bad = arange(6).reshape(4, 2); print(bad.len()) } catch e { caught = caught + 1; print("caught: " + e.to(str)) }
    print(caught)
    var ok = arange(6).reshape(2, 3)
    print(ok.shape[0].to(int))
    return 0
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "rust", provider: "py" }
exit: 0
error-kind: "python.5"
error-span: "76..99"

#### stdout

```text
caught: PyException ValueError: cannot reshape array of size 6 into shape (4,2)
1
2
```

### Probe a2py
recipe: "ac-a2py/hir-stdlib-run-v1"
profile: "python-script"
entry: "main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource"]
exit: 0
error-type: "ValueError"
error-kind: "python.5"
error-span: "76..99"

#### stdout
compare: "lf"

```text
caught: PyException ValueError: cannot reshape array of size 6 into shape (4,2)
1
2
value:0
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

The real NumPy `ValueError` (class 5) raised by `arange(6).reshape(4, 2)`
unwinds into the Auto handler EXACTLY ONCE (`caught` prints `1`; the
`bad.len()` print is skipped), and execution continues: the valid reshape
still runs and prints its first axis. `[76,99)` is the half-open byte range
of the failing call expression in the author source.

## Case: json-decode-error-uncaught
id: "py.libraries.1126.json-decode-error-uncaught"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1126"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.as"
syntax: "auto-script"

```auto
use.py json: loads
fn main() int {
    var data = loads("{")
    return data["values"].len()
}
```

